  "design_notes": "Warden reads as a 2.4 m upright post: a tall unbroken navy pillar body, square silver shoulder caps and a flat-topped helmet box, with long rigid two-segment arms hanging straight to mid-thigh, so its silhouette is a sign-post rather than a figure. Every shape is a right angle and every joint lines up on a straight vertical axis, expressing a mind that follows the literal text of an order and nothing beside it; the single horizontal visor bar is a ruled line that can only tilt or thin, which makes its final faint smile land. Its heavy square feet and evenly spaced knee plates set up its measured, arriving walk. The colour story is the uniform of Gridhaven authority: deep navy paint with polished silver trim that echoes the city's steel blue, a cold white visor, and a square chest badge lamp that is the only place the Board's verdict shows, switching between green and red."
}